WEBVTT

00:01:55.198 --> 00:01:56.449
Oh, crap.

00:01:56.449 --> 00:02:01.329
Bound for JFK Airport. The door is closing.

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:27.897
You're making too much of a fuss.

00:02:27.897 --> 00:02:30.275
Hey, miracle boy,

00:02:30.275 --> 00:02:32.193
you dropped something.

00:02:33.278 --> 00:02:34.279
Thanks.

00:02:41.244 --> 00:02:43.621
Japan, huh?

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:51.796
"The Return of the Prince"

00:02:57.052 --> 00:02:59.429
Did you hear about the middle schoolers?

00:02:59.429 --> 00:03:02.265
Yeah, what kind of joke is that?

00:03:02.265 --> 00:03:05.643
They won't last three days at this camp.

00:03:05.935 --> 00:03:08.897
I guess we'll have to take care of them.

00:03:23.995 --> 00:03:27.749
So this is the U-17 selection camp.

00:03:27.749 --> 00:03:30.293
I-It looks pretty intense.

00:03:31.002 --> 00:03:36.174
Is it really okay that we were invited here?

00:03:36.633 --> 00:03:38.093
Zero percent okay.

00:03:38.843 --> 00:03:43.473
Until last year, no middle schooler
had ever been invited to this camp.

00:03:43.807 --> 00:03:47.143
Probability there is a catch: 100%.

00:03:47.143 --> 00:03:48.937
Check it out!

00:03:48.937 --> 00:03:50.647
It's a security camera.

00:03:50.647 --> 00:03:51.189
Yay.

00:03:51.189 --> 00:03:53.108
Eiji, cut that out!

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:56.152
Don't walk in front of me!

00:03:56.152 --> 00:04:00.490
You're the one who needs to
stop obstructing my path!

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:01.950
It's stinking hot!

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:04.202
And you're just stinking!

00:04:04.202 --> 00:04:05.620
You wanna fight? Huh?

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:07.664
Bring it on!

00:04:09.666 --> 00:04:12.377
Enough, you two.

00:04:12.377 --> 00:04:14.504
We didn't come here to fight.

00:04:16.172 --> 00:04:17.132
Let's go.

00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:21.302
Hold it right there, boys.

00:04:21.803 --> 00:04:23.304
You're them, right?

00:04:23.638 --> 00:04:26.349
The super middle schoolers who've been

00:04:26.349 --> 00:04:28.727
extended a special invitation to come here?

00:04:28.727 --> 00:04:33.231
I know you just got here,
but there's a test.

00:04:33.648 --> 00:04:35.150
A test?

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:41.156
You'll each get five balls.

00:04:41.156 --> 00:04:44.367
You will pass if you can
knock over those three cans.

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:45.660
What's the matter?

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.245
You don't look too happy.

00:04:48.496 --> 00:04:49.789
Hey, now...

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:53.335
If you can't even manage
this, you don't belong here.

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:56.254
What?

00:04:56.254 --> 00:04:57.547
Already?

00:04:57.547 --> 00:05:00.258
Oh, lucky. I got one.

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:03.178
Here comes another.

00:05:06.181 --> 00:05:08.475
The Seishun Academy tennis club.

00:05:08.475 --> 00:05:11.019
The champions of this year's
national tournament.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.361
Takeshi Momoshiro, second year.

00:05:19.736 --> 00:05:23.740
Possesses powerful offensive
ability and calm insight.

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:27.327
Special moves: Dunk Smash, Jack Knife.

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:29.496
Burning!

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:32.832
Takashi Kawamura, third year.

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:36.961
Facing opponents head on with his
exceptional power is his philosophy.

00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:39.339
Special move: Hadoukyu.

00:05:39.339 --> 00:05:41.341
Great!

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:46.179
His personality changes
when he holds a racquet.

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:56.106
I got some good data.

00:05:56.106 --> 00:05:58.525
Sadaharu Inui, third year.

00:05:58.525 --> 00:06:01.236
An intellectual who reads the
game with his data tennis.

00:06:01.236 --> 00:06:03.822
His special move is the Waterfall.

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:07.242
Kaoru Kaidoh, second year.

00:06:07.659 --> 00:06:11.871
His tenacious play style has
earned him the nickname "Viper."

00:06:18.003 --> 00:06:19.546
He possesses the ability

00:06:19.546 --> 00:06:21.589
to hit curving shots like
his Boomerang Snake.

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:24.718
I was wondering how they would respond

00:06:24.718 --> 00:06:29.514
to the teasing of some hot-headed
high schoolers, but...

00:06:30.098 --> 00:06:32.726
It seems they're not half bad.

00:06:35.729 --> 00:06:37.480
There's the Moon Volley!

00:06:38.523 --> 00:06:39.399
There.

00:06:41.568 --> 00:06:45.155
Shuichiroh Oishi, Eiji Kikumaru, third years.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:49.075
The Moon Volleys that Oishi
deals with his precise control

00:06:49.701 --> 00:06:55.790
and Kikumaru's acrobatic play, make them
Seishun Academy's Golden Pair in doubles.

00:07:03.256 --> 00:07:05.592
Shusuke Fuji, third year.

00:07:06.009 --> 00:07:08.136
A prodigal player with a variety of skills

00:07:08.136 --> 00:07:11.389
including Tsubame Gaeshi, the Swallow Return,
and Hakugei, the White Whale.

00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:14.100
Tezuka, you only need one ball, right?

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.018
Yeah.

00:07:21.733 --> 00:07:23.651
All three with only one ball.

00:07:24.152 --> 00:07:25.070
Impressive.

00:07:26.196 --> 00:07:28.615
Kunimitsu Tezuka, third year.

00:07:29.115 --> 00:07:31.576
Seishun Academy tennis club captain.

00:07:32.202 --> 00:07:39.000
Rumor has it, his flawless ability
assures his place in the real world.

00:07:39.417 --> 00:07:41.044
All right, guys.

00:07:41.044 --> 00:07:42.921
Coming through.

00:07:43.213 --> 00:07:46.216
Too bad. Try again next week.

00:07:57.018 --> 00:07:59.312
It's state of the art.

00:07:59.312 --> 00:08:02.315
This U-17 selection camp...

00:08:02.315 --> 00:08:06.736
...produces elite tennis players
ready for the real world.

00:08:07.487 --> 00:08:09.948
The training is intense.

00:08:10.532 --> 00:08:14.369
Over half of all participants
drop out within a week.

00:08:14.869 --> 00:08:18.623
There are stories of promising
athletes who fail here

00:08:18.623 --> 00:08:21.543
and give up on tennis.

00:08:22.419 --> 00:08:26.381
I'm not sure why we were summoned here.

00:08:26.965 --> 00:08:31.219
However, now that we're here,
we'll see this through.

00:08:32.053 --> 00:08:34.139
All eight of us.

00:08:35.557 --> 00:08:38.059
All eight, huh?

00:08:38.977 --> 00:08:42.480
If Echizen were here, there'd be nine.

00:08:52.824 --> 00:08:56.828
Those poor middle schoolers.

00:08:56.828 --> 00:08:59.622
They're gonna learn the meaning
of failure at such a young age.

00:08:59.622 --> 00:09:01.875
You should worry about yourself.

00:09:01.875 --> 00:09:04.669
Court 13, no talking.

00:09:05.337 --> 00:09:08.757
Todoroki, Murata, you're
demoted to Court 14.

00:09:09.341 --> 00:09:10.216
Yes, sir.

00:09:13.595 --> 00:09:15.221
Nice to meet you.

00:09:15.221 --> 00:09:16.931
I am Strategic Coach Kurobe,

00:09:16.931 --> 00:09:22.020
tasked with directing this camp
while the director is absent.

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:28.735
Gentlemen, as you know, we have
invited fifty middle schoolers

00:09:28.735 --> 00:09:32.530
to join the 246 high schoolers here.

00:09:33.406 --> 00:09:34.616
Fifty?

00:09:35.492 --> 00:09:38.870
Beginning now, whether you're a
middle schooler or high schooler,

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:44.042
we will hone your skills and
raise the bar of the U-17.

00:09:45.168 --> 00:09:48.380
However, I have a message from the director.

00:09:49.089 --> 00:09:51.091
"300 is too many."

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:54.719
"Drop 250 balls."

00:09:55.011 --> 00:10:00.809
"Send those unable to get a ball away."

00:10:00.809 --> 00:10:01.559
Seriously?!

00:10:01.559 --> 00:10:03.436
That's ridiculous!

00:10:04.187 --> 00:10:04.938
The balls!

00:10:04.938 --> 00:10:06.272
Get the balls!

00:10:07.065 --> 00:10:08.733
Don't let your guard down.

00:10:14.823 --> 00:10:15.740
You're...

00:10:25.625 --> 00:10:27.669
You're all here.

00:10:27.919 --> 00:10:33.425
Did you really think they'd invite
you rabble and not invite the king?

00:10:34.426 --> 00:10:38.263
You must be going soft not
to realize we're here.

00:10:38.513 --> 00:10:41.766
Kansai players are eligible for selection, too.

00:10:41.766 --> 00:10:43.685
Koshimae's not here?

00:10:43.935 --> 00:10:46.021
If you're arrogant enough to think

00:10:46.021 --> 00:10:47.647
you're the only ones who've been chosen,

00:10:47.647 --> 00:10:49.107
I'll force feed you bitter melon.

00:10:49.399 --> 00:10:55.030
Just because we're all middle schoolers,
it doesn't make us friends.

00:11:03.747 --> 00:11:04.831
Where are the balls?

00:11:04.831 --> 00:11:06.124
There's none left!

00:11:06.124 --> 00:11:07.125
You're kidding!

00:11:07.125 --> 00:11:08.668
There's gotta be one somewhere!

00:11:09.586 --> 00:11:11.087
Poke, poke.

00:11:34.694 --> 00:11:35.779
Hey.

00:11:43.036 --> 00:11:43.912
Hey.

00:11:44.287 --> 00:11:45.205
Echizen!

00:11:45.789 --> 00:11:47.123
Don't "hey" me!

00:11:47.123 --> 00:11:48.541
Shorty!

00:11:48.541 --> 00:11:52.629
I can't breathe, Momo-<i>senpai</i>.
That hurts, Eiji-<i>senpai</i>.

00:11:52.629 --> 00:11:54.839
We were worried about you, Echizen.

00:11:54.839 --> 00:11:56.758
You disappeared all of a sudden.

00:11:56.758 --> 00:12:00.303
Probability of Echizen being invited: 120%.

00:12:00.303 --> 00:12:01.680
Just as the data suggested.

00:12:02.597 --> 00:12:04.391
Welcome back!

00:12:04.391 --> 00:12:05.517
Welcome back.

00:12:05.517 --> 00:12:06.559
Thanks.

00:12:06.851 --> 00:12:08.978
How was America?

00:12:10.271 --> 00:12:11.398
It was all right.

00:12:11.398 --> 00:12:13.775
This is great, Momo.

00:12:13.775 --> 00:12:15.652
Now there's nine of us.

00:12:15.652 --> 00:12:18.113
I... I wasn't...

00:12:19.239 --> 00:12:20.240
Everyone's here.

00:12:24.828 --> 00:12:27.038
That boy hasn't changed.

00:12:28.248 --> 00:12:30.542
You haven't gotten worse, have you?

00:12:30.542 --> 00:12:32.502
You must be going soft, to show up so late.

00:12:32.752 --> 00:12:34.087
Koshimae!

00:12:34.587 --> 00:12:36.256
Let's go!

00:12:37.048 --> 00:12:38.299
Is that all you ever want to do?

00:12:38.675 --> 00:12:43.346
It seems all the middle
schoolers acquired a ball.

00:12:44.139 --> 00:12:48.268
Allow me to explain how this camp works.

00:12:49.269 --> 00:12:54.399
Participants are divided between
Courts 1 to 16 by skill.

00:12:54.733 --> 00:12:57.527
The smaller the number,
the stronger the players.

00:12:57.944 --> 00:13:00.196
Every day, before practice,

00:13:00.196 --> 00:13:03.533
the coaches will divide you into groups

00:13:03.533 --> 00:13:05.744
to play against each other in shuffle matches.

00:13:06.327 --> 00:13:06.619
Winners will move up a court.

00:13:06.619 --> 00:13:08.038
"8 players (Court 1-3)" "12 players (Court 4-6)"
"16 players (Court 7-8)" "9 players (Court 9)"
Winners will move up a court.

00:13:08.038 --> 00:13:10.498
"8 players (Court 1-3)" "12 players (Court 4-6)"
"16 players (Court 7-8)" "9 players (Court 9)"
Losers will move down a court.

00:13:10.707 --> 00:13:15.587
The only way to move up is to
win in those shuffle matches.

00:13:17.422 --> 00:13:20.258
High schoolers who did not
manage to get a ball...

00:13:20.258 --> 00:13:22.969
As instructed, you are to leave immediately.

00:13:23.803 --> 00:13:24.929
That is all.

00:13:24.929 --> 00:13:27.557
Hold it, you little runts!

00:13:27.557 --> 00:13:30.602
You can't pick up more than one ball!

00:13:30.602 --> 00:13:32.854
He didn't say we couldn't.

00:13:32.854 --> 00:13:34.898
That's right! Finder's keepers!

00:13:36.441 --> 00:13:37.442
Too bad!

00:13:37.442 --> 00:13:39.319
Now beat it!

00:13:39.861 --> 00:13:43.073
Don't get ahead of yourself
just because you got a ball.

00:13:43.656 --> 00:13:46.743
That's got nothing to do with tennis.

00:13:47.869 --> 00:13:49.329
A match.

00:13:49.329 --> 00:13:51.289
Let's settle this with a match.

00:13:51.623 --> 00:13:53.625
You don't know when to give up.

00:13:53.875 --> 00:13:55.877
You, four eyes!

00:13:55.877 --> 00:13:58.463
I'll play you for your ball!

00:14:00.799 --> 00:14:03.009
Hold on, Tezuka-<i>kun</i>.

00:14:03.009 --> 00:14:05.804
He was talking to me.

00:14:06.304 --> 00:14:08.848
No, Kite-<i>kun</i>, he was talking to me.

00:14:09.474 --> 00:14:12.394
Four eyes has gotta be me, right?

00:14:13.937 --> 00:14:16.940
Why are you taking off your
glasses, Inui-<i>senpai</i>?

00:14:17.357 --> 00:14:18.942
Come on, you...

00:14:18.942 --> 00:14:20.860
Ready?

00:14:23.488 --> 00:14:26.241
Echizen, where'd you get those glasses?

00:14:27.033 --> 00:14:29.411
Huh? When did you...

00:14:29.411 --> 00:14:32.831
My glasses! My glasses!

00:14:32.831 --> 00:14:33.832
Thanks.

00:14:34.916 --> 00:14:36.668
You're so mean!

00:14:37.043 --> 00:14:40.213
You again? Stay out of this, kid!

00:14:41.381 --> 00:14:44.843
You're all talk, aren't you?

00:14:44.843 --> 00:14:45.719
What?

00:14:45.719 --> 00:14:48.054
Sasabe, let me handle this.

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:51.599
Matsudaira.

00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:58.732
He's just a kid. Go somewhat easy on him.

00:14:58.732 --> 00:14:59.816
Unfortunately...

00:15:01.359 --> 00:15:05.405
I don't know how to take it easy.

00:15:06.197 --> 00:15:08.783
That's fine. You don't need to go easy.

00:15:09.075 --> 00:15:10.827
Either way, I'll win.

00:15:14.789 --> 00:15:16.082
Magnum!

00:15:19.586 --> 00:15:20.587
Close one!

00:15:21.046 --> 00:15:24.007
He almost got him right in the face!

00:15:24.299 --> 00:15:26.134
Beat the crap out of him!

00:15:34.434 --> 00:15:36.019
Magnum!

00:15:37.979 --> 00:15:39.105
H-He returned it.

00:15:39.773 --> 00:15:41.816
This should be fun!

00:15:56.373 --> 00:16:00.043
Matsudaira, how long are
you gonna play with him?

00:16:00.293 --> 00:16:01.836
Finish it already!

00:16:01.836 --> 00:16:03.588
We're waiting!

00:16:03.588 --> 00:16:05.256
Hey, guys!

00:16:05.256 --> 00:16:07.425
Shouldn't one of you sub in for him?

00:16:07.425 --> 00:16:09.552
Shorty's gonna cry!

00:16:09.552 --> 00:16:12.722
Or maybe you're all scared!

00:16:13.807 --> 00:16:16.434
There's no need for us to sub in.

00:16:16.434 --> 00:16:19.562
Magnum? Pathetic.

00:16:19.896 --> 00:16:21.981
It's nothing more than a pachinko ball.

00:16:22.565 --> 00:16:24.401
This kid...

00:16:30.031 --> 00:16:33.785
He's toying with me by copying my shots.

00:16:43.169 --> 00:16:44.212
Hey.

00:16:45.296 --> 00:16:47.716
That serve was pretty interesting.

00:16:47.716 --> 00:16:48.383
What?

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:50.468
That stance...

00:17:00.854 --> 00:17:03.648
Th-That's my Magnum Serve!

00:17:14.743 --> 00:17:16.661
You still have a long way to go.

00:17:19.205 --> 00:17:22.625
The Silver Hadoukyu reaches 108!

00:17:25.003 --> 00:17:27.630
Ahh... Ecstasy.

00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:29.382
That's the power of the Bible!

00:17:29.382 --> 00:17:31.968
They can't touch Shiraishi!

00:17:40.268 --> 00:17:42.729
A-Are you sure?

00:17:42.729 --> 00:17:44.564
Thanks.

00:17:44.564 --> 00:17:45.732
Not at all.

00:17:47.901 --> 00:17:49.319
You moron!

00:17:49.778 --> 00:17:52.614
Don't help your enemies, Chotaro!

00:17:52.947 --> 00:17:54.240
That's lame!

00:17:54.616 --> 00:17:57.911
Huh? Shishido-<i>senpai</i>, what'd you say?

00:17:57.911 --> 00:17:59.329
I said it's lame.

00:17:59.746 --> 00:18:01.998
Not super lame?

00:18:02.415 --> 00:18:04.834
Just plain lame.

00:18:12.050 --> 00:18:14.886
Are these guys really middle schoolers?

00:18:20.725 --> 00:18:23.520
I can see all your blind spots!

00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:25.438
As swift as lightning!

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:34.406
Rikkai's Sanada-<i>kun </i>and...

00:18:35.156 --> 00:18:37.575
Hyotei's Atobe-<i>kun</i>.

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:42.038
These middle schoolers seem quite good.

00:18:43.415 --> 00:18:46.584
It's still too early to tell.

00:18:52.799 --> 00:18:54.843
I'm just getting started.

00:18:55.468 --> 00:18:56.344
Hey!

00:18:56.344 --> 00:18:57.679
Someone give me a racquet!

00:18:57.679 --> 00:18:59.264
You're pathetic!

00:18:59.889 --> 00:19:04.477
How foolish to challenge an
opponent of unknown strength.

00:19:04.477 --> 00:19:07.689
If you didn't get a ball, get out of here!

00:19:08.523 --> 00:19:11.109
I won't allow this abomination to continue!

00:19:11.693 --> 00:19:13.778
Bro...

00:19:17.449 --> 00:19:20.952
What? You're leaving? Wait!

00:19:21.244 --> 00:19:23.121
I haven't played yet!

00:19:23.872 --> 00:19:24.831
Sorry about that.

00:19:26.249 --> 00:19:29.711
You can't play matches
here without permission.

00:19:30.045 --> 00:19:34.424
If you want to play against us,
win your shuffle matches.

00:19:34.424 --> 00:19:39.387
Don't be ridiculous. You
high schoolers started it.

00:19:39.387 --> 00:19:41.014
Just so you know,

00:19:41.014 --> 00:19:45.352
the people you played against
were all Court 10 or lower.

00:19:45.352 --> 00:19:46.770
Don't get ahead of yourself.

00:19:48.188 --> 00:19:52.859
Then what court are you, you puppet?

00:19:53.401 --> 00:19:56.488
I'll crush you right now.

00:19:57.822 --> 00:19:59.824
Don't get ahead of yourself.

00:20:00.575 --> 00:20:03.745
Who do you think you're ordering around?

00:20:03.995 --> 00:20:04.704
Akutsu.

00:20:04.704 --> 00:20:07.165
The shuffle matches should be fun.

00:20:07.999 --> 00:20:11.127
I'm Kanata Irie from Court 3.

00:20:13.171 --> 00:20:16.007
Court 5, Jujiroh Oni.

00:20:18.635 --> 00:20:22.347
We look forward to playing against you.

00:20:26.226 --> 00:20:28.103
What number are you?

00:20:29.521 --> 00:20:31.523
What's wrong with you? Can't you...

00:20:44.536 --> 00:20:45.704
Do you want to go home?

00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:02.721
Kazuya Tokugawa, Court 1.

00:21:06.266 --> 00:21:07.934
It would seem there are

00:21:07.934 --> 00:21:11.146
greater monsters here
than we initially thought.

00:21:13.231 --> 00:21:18.820
Regardless if this is a den of
monsters or even hell,

00:21:18.820 --> 00:21:20.530
we'll see this through to the end,

00:21:21.364 --> 00:21:24.868
every last one of us.

00:21:31.458 --> 00:21:34.336
Ooh... This should be interesting.

00:23:17.063 --> 00:23:18.064
"Preview"

00:23:18.064 --> 00:23:20.608
"Preview"
The shuffle matches are about
to start, Momo-<i>senpai</i>.

00:23:20.608 --> 00:23:23.361
Yeah, I can't wait. I can't wait.

00:23:23.361 --> 00:23:28.158
I heard your opponent, Oni,
is so strong he can lift boulders.

00:23:28.158 --> 00:23:28.908
Boulders?

00:23:28.908 --> 00:23:30.910
That's inhuman!

00:23:30.910 --> 00:23:33.663
But it does mean he's a
power player, just like me.

00:23:33.663 --> 00:23:36.583
I can't lose.

00:23:36.583 --> 00:23:38.501
Win and jump all the way to Court 5.

00:23:38.501 --> 00:23:39.377
Yeah!

00:23:41.755 --> 00:23:42.797
"The Guardian of Hell"
The next episode of <i>Prince of</i>
<i>Tennis II </i>is: "The Guardian of Hell."

00:23:42.797 --> 00:23:47.094
"The Guardian of Hell"
I'm off to slay me an Oni!
